# Keep the build context small and never ship host artifacts.
#
# The second half of this list is about what the running image serves. `COPY
# web/` takes the whole document root, and web/test/ lives inside it — so the
# deployment was serving nineteen test files, including the end-to-end ones
# that spell out the admin permission model. The static layer refuses those
# paths now (see allowedPath in server/src/app.ts); this is the other half,
# and the better one: what is not in the image cannot be served by any future
# misconfiguration.

**/node_modules
.git
*.log
docs/screenshots

# --- tests: needed by CI from the repository, never by the running image ---
web/test
server/test

# --- development and CI scaffolding ---
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.md
!README.md
docs
